    "result_text": "The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure-based membership level 4 rule in the Spring Boot pet clinic application.\n\n**Changes in `Owner.java`:**\n- `getMembershipLevel()` now keeps the pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) **capped at 3**, then adds a 4th level only when the owner's tenure exceeds 365 days. A newly created owner has zero tenure, so it can never reach 4 \u2014 matching the spec's example (email + `namesakeCount` 0 + 3-member household \u2192 level 3).\n- Added a `getTenureDays()` helper that returns whole days from `registrationDate` to the current date (`null` when no registration date), with `ChronoUnit.DAYS`.\n- Updated the Javadoc on both methods and added the `java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit` import.\n\n**Changes in `openapi.yml`:**\n- Updated the `membershipLevel` description to document the tenure-over-365-days rule and raised `maximum` from 3 to 4.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3`) passes \u2014 a new owner with an email and no namesake lands at level 3, not 4 \u2014 and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
