    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the existing structure of `Owner` cleanly:\n\n- **Right unit.** The tenure logic lives alongside the other derived read-only getters (`getAgeBand`, `getMembershipNumber`, `getCheckDigit`, `getLocality`), which is exactly where membership derivation already lives. No new catch-all is being created.\n- **Good decomposition.** Extracting `getTenureDays()` as its own getter rather than inlining `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(...)` into `getMembershipLevel()` matches the codebase's convention of exposing each meaningful derived value as its own documented accessor, and makes the \"> 365 days\" threshold self-describing. No duplication \u2014 the single source of the tenure value is reused.\n- **Idiomatic null handling.** `getTenureDays()` returns `null` when `registrationDate` is absent and the caller null-checks before using it, consistent with the null-on-missing-input pattern used by every sibling getter.\n- **Docs kept coherent.** The javadoc, the cross-references (`{@link #getTenureDays()}`), the `@return` range (now 1\u20134), and the OpenAPI `maximum`/description were all updated together, so the contract stays in sync.\n\nA maintainer of this class would find this natural and additive.",
